2650	{"artifactId":"ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72","entry":{"id":"e3cc9959","text":"ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE: two more variants of the same misfiling, both observed on 2026-10-04 while building the fix for ISSUE-605c70574633ed67 (an ISSUE-anchored small bugfix built with sizeClass 'trivial'). Filed here rather than as new issues because the fault is the same: a writer derives the work item's folder from something other than the item's own definition and siblings, so its record lands in a second folder.\n\nVARIANT 2 - BUILD record, wrong DATE segment. The implement and validate turns wrote BUILD.md to docs/standalone/bug-docs-review-pane-s-opendoc-E20261004605c7057/S001/, while the ISSUE (created 2026-10-01) sits in docs/standalone/bug-docs-review-pane-s-opendoc-E20261001605c7057/. This record DID carry standalone:true and sizeClass, and the slug was right; only the E<date> anchor differed. The record's meta.createdAt was 2026-10-04T09:40:27Z. Reading buildRecordFolderArgs in src/workflow/storage.ts: on the standalone branch the anchor comes from the story's LLD and falls back to the record's own createdAt; a trivial-sized bugfix has no LLD, so the anchor is the build's own clock rather than the ISSUE's createdAt. The label on that same branch IS read from the definition head, which is why the slug was correct and only the date forked. Not verified by a test.\n\nVARIANT 3 - code-review record, wrong top-level folder and raw-hash name. insrc_code_review_step for the same story wrote CR.md to docs/epics/605c70574633ed67-E20261004605c7057/S001/CR.md: epics instead of standalone, the epic hash instead of the slug, and today's date instead of the issue's. This matches the symptom of the original observation in this issue but on the code-review writer, not the BUILD writer, and for a story that HAS a definition head (the ISSUE). The cause was not traced in the code; ISSUE-b2e16601ad94f39b records that the CR writer takes its label from the LLD's stored meta, and with no LLD that would be empty, which is consistent with this but unconfirmed.\n\nBoth records were moved by hand beside the ISSUE in commit 82e070b.\n\nScope note for whoever picks this up: the original report covers an LLD-only story with no definition head; these two cover a definition-head story with no LLD. A fix that only teaches the lookup to fall back to the LLD would not cover variants 2 and 3.","actor":{"id":"legacy:claude-opus-5-5-controller","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"claude-opus-5.5 (controller)"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-04T09:51:04.000Z","feedback":[],"kind":"revision-request","anchor":{"section":".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72.json"}}}
